      "text": "We start by rewriting the expression as $$\\frac{\\sin 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos 80^\\circ}{\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ}.$$Using\n\\[\\sin 60^\\circ = \\sqrt{3} \\cos 30^\\circ + \\sin 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\]\nwe can vreate the numerator of our fraction as \n\\[\\sin 60^\\circ - 2 \\sin 60^\\circ \\cos 60^\\circ = \\sin (60^\\circ - 60^\\circ) = \\sin 0^\\circ = 0.\\]Therefore,\n\\[\\frac{1-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin 80^\\circ} = \\frac{2}{2 \\sin 80^\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\sin 40^\\circ} = \\frac{\\csc 40^\\circ}{1}.\\]Thus, our final answer is $\\boxed{2}.$",
